---
description: MindCraft project rules — kid-safe browser voxel game, no backend, data-driven blocks
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root: it holds the rules and links every playbook.

Never negotiable: kid-safe (no damage, monsters, weapons, failure); no network at
runtime, no accounts, no tracking; blocks are data and their numeric ids are permanent;
every world edit goes through a `Command` so Undo works; every capability is a tool
(`domain_verb`) in the one registry; keyboard, touch and gamepad all work; old saves
keep loading; anything a kid can ask for in words works with no model downloaded.

`npm run lint` is the typecheck — a bare `npx tsc --noEmit` checks nothing here.
